==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=fitness}}

===Etymology===
{{suffix|fit|ness}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-fitness.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{IPA|/ˈfɪtnəs/}}
* {{rhymes|ɪtnəs}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|es}}

# The condition of being [[fit]], [[suitable]] or [[appropriate]].
# The cultivation of an attractive and/or healthy physique.
#* {{quote-news
|year=2011
|date=April 11
|author=Phil McNulty
|title=Liverpool 3 - 0 Man City
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9449111.stm
|page=
|passage=Carroll has been edging slowly towards full '''fitness''' after his expensive arrival from Newcastle United and his partnership with £23m Luis Suarez showed rich promise as Liverpool controlled affairs from start to finish.}}
# {{context|UK|slang|lang=en}} The condition of being [[attractive]], [[fanciable]] or [[beautiful]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|cultivation of an attractive and/or healthy physique}} [[beauty]], [[health]]
* {{sense|condition of being suitable}} [[strength]], [[suitability]], [[competence]], [[capability]]
* {{sense|condition of being attractive}} see [[Wikisaurus:sexy]]

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|cultivation of an attractive and/or healthy physique}} [[flab]], [[sloth]]
* {{sense|ability to perform}} [[weakness]]

